(text "24 V BUS (red): bench supply + -> F0 -> VM on every driver. Ground return (black): every driver GND -> bench supply -" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 205.74 106.68 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 5a5e5714-b35b-42eb-be73-6a6b13ef9839))
(text "NOTES\n1. Mega pins: STEP D22-26, DIR D30-34, EN D36-40 (LOW = driver on; 10k pull-ups keep drivers OFF while the Mega boots), encoders A0-A4, gripper PWM D9, tool I2C D20-D21.\n2. TMC2209 standalone mode: UART mode: MS1/MS2 set each driver bus address (0-2), microstep is set over UART. CLK = GND selects the internal clock.\n3. Check pin names against the silkscreen of the TMC2209 modules you buy (vendors differ). Set phase current with the module trimmer before connecting the arm.\n4. TMC2209 VM max is about 29 V: 24 V only. Never plug or unplug a motor with 24 V present. Verify coil pairs with an ohmmeter.\n5. Modules sit in female headers on perfboard. Heatsink on every module, 40 mm fan over the row.\n6. All grounds common. Never connect 24 V or 6 V to the Mega 5 V pins." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 40.64 535.94 0) (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left top)) (uuid 2b8c24f1-df3f-47b3-9fd1-2f1562f400f0))
(text "BILL OF MATERIALS (electrical parts; full list, links and prices in hardware/bom)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 30.48 358.14 0) (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left top)) (uuid 57ea87e8-d019-4e3c-a441-279885648585))
(text "Ref\nU1\nPS2\nU2\nPS1\nDRV1-DRV5\nM1, M3\nM2\nM4\nM5\nM7\nJ6\nU6\nENC1-ENC5\nF0-F2\nSW1\nK1\nD1\nC7, C20-C24\nC1-C5, C8\nR1-R5, R13, R21-R25, R31-R32\nFAN1" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 30.48 363.22 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 28939d19-6404-4abf-a147-4c747207097d))
(text "Qty\n1\n1\n1\n1\n5\n2\n1\n1\n1\n1\n1\n1\n5\n3\n1\n1\n1\n6\n6\n13\n1" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 60.96 363.22 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 027236b4-7d48-418f-a213-189905216457))
(text "Part\nRaspberry Pi 5 8GB\nOfficial Raspberry Pi 27 W USB-C supply\nArduino Mega 2560 R3\n24 V supply\nBIGTREETECH TMC2209 V1.3 + heatsink\nSTEPPERONLINE 17HS19-1684S-PG5\nSTEPPERONLINE 17HS19-1684S-PG14\nSTEPPERONLINE 17HS08-1004S\nSTEPPERONLINE 11HS20-0674S\nMG996R servo\nGX12 6-pin tool plug\nXL4015 5 A buck module, set 6.0 V\nAS5600 magnetic encoder module + diametric magnet\nInline ATO fuse holders, 10 A, 2 A and 3 A fuses\nE-stop, 22 mm latching mushroom, 1 NC\n24 V coil relay, normally open, with socket\n1N4007 flyback diode\nElectrolytic 1000 uF 16 V (x1), 100 uF 35 V (x5)\nCeramic 100 nF\n1k (x8), 10k (x5) metal film 1/4 W\n40 mm 5 V fan over driver row" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 71.12 363.22 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 0bba69ce-c8d7-4312-83a9-03b55f61b1ed))
(text "Note\nowned\nowned\nowned\nowned\n\nJ1, J3\nJ2\nJ4\nJ5\nJ6 gripper tool\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 162.56 363.22 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid ceb60f5f-5b58-4684-82ba-cb43bc0e540c))
